# Local env. Every .env file is local — Vite reads plain `.env` as well as
# `.env.local`, and the first spelling was not covered here, so a referrer
# address written to the obvious filename would have been committed.
# `.env.example` is the exception: it is the template and carries no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
